Communion: How Lovely is Your Dwelling Place

>Intro:G D Em C G G7
d b d.   d e d a a   b g

Chorus:
>   G              D
How lovely is Your dwelling place,
> Em          C            G
O Lord mighty God, Lord of all.


I.
>D             C             Em           D
Even the lowly sparrow finds a home for her brood
>        D           C
And the swallow a nest for herself
>     Em      D         C
Where she may lay here young
>       Am         F   C       D
In your altars my king and my God (Repeat Chorus)



Chorus:
>   G              D
How lovely is Your dwelling place,
> Em          C            G
O Lord mighty God, Lord of all.


II. same chords as I

>D               C    
Blessed are they whose dwelling
>        Em       D    
Is Your  own Lord of peace
>               D         C            
Blest are they refreshed by springs and by rain
>        Em       D       C
When dryness daunts and scathes
>       Am         F   C       D
Behold my shield, my king and my God! (Repeat Chorus)



Chorus:
>   G              D
How lovely is Your dwelling place,
> Em          C            G
O Lord mighty God, Lord of all.

III.
>D                  C             Em      D
I would forsake a thousand other days anywhere
>  D                  C
If I could spend one day in Your Courts
> Em      D     C        Em          D     C
belong to you alone, My strength are You alone
>   Am        F    C     D
My glory, my king and my God! (Repeat Chorus)


Chorus:
>   G              D
How lovely is Your dwelling place,
> Em          C            G
O Lord mighty God, Lord of all.

Coda:
>     C            G
How lovely.. Your dwelling place
> Em            D             G
O Lord.. mighty God, Lord of all.






